# Wolseley 18/85 four-door saloon, 1938-1948.
#
# The 2,321 cc six of the 1938 Wolseley range, on the same 2.654 m wheelbase
# as the 14/60 and 16/65 but with the wider body. Production stopped for the
# war and resumed in 1945.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wolseley_18/85
#
# Dimensions 4.369 x 1.702 x 1.676 m, wheelbase 2.654 m.
#
# Shape reference: NO true level side profile exists. Image 1 is a front
# three-quarter about 30 degrees off square; the flank is estimated from it
# and the other views within the published dimensions. The limitation is
# recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no period chart was found. Black, grey, green and
# maroon are plain names. Weights 15, 13, 12, 10, total 50, provisional.
#
# Speed 130 km/h. Comfort 60/420, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 60. Classes 2,3.
# Dates are road presence: 1938 intro, retires staggered 1958-1961.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/wolseley-18-85.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/wolseley-18-85.dae. References:
# citycars/references/wolseley-18-85/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: there is no true side or rear view, so the flank and tail
# are estimated. The police roof sign was omitted, and the wing-to-running-board
# transitions and rear fittings are simplified. At 128 px the wide six-light body
# and Wolseley grille read as an 18/85.


obj=citycar
name=Wolseley1885(Black)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=15
intro_year=1938
intro_month=9
retire_year=1961
retire_month=6
speed=130
